            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Bilateral anterior thigh pain may indicate bacteremia (Louria's Sign). We present a case of Ehrlichiosis due to Ehrlichia chaffeensis whose predominant presenting symptom was localized bilateral anterior thigh pain.</AbstractText>
